IMPORT prelude

-- International Organisations (Immunities and Privileges) Act 1948 (Singapore) -- which organisations the Act reaches
-- (s 2(1), First Schedule), what an order may give an organisation (s 2(2)(a), Second Schedule Part 1), who among its people
-- may be given immunity and how far (s 2(2)(b), (c), Second Schedule Parts 2 to 4), the limit set by the proviso to s 2(2),
-- the Gazette lists (s 2(3)), conference delegates (s 3), the International Court under s 4(b), and reciprocity (s 5).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation ("version in force from 6/1/2025"), as deposited at
-- ../../registers/source-bundle/IOIPA1948.txt. The latest amendment annotated is S 4/2025 wef 06/01/2025, which added the
-- Organisation for Economic Co-operation and Development to the First Schedule.
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Requirement REQ-0142 in ../../../requirements.jsonl: Tier 2 of the remaining Singapore Acts, ordered by
-- everyday-life relevance. It asks what the Act decides for a person or business it applies to; no scenario has asked a
-- sharper question yet. For an ordinary person or business the question is usually "can I sue this organisation, or this
-- person who works for it?" The Act is short (6 sections and two Schedules) and is encoded nearly whole. Not encoded: the
-- short title (s 1), the Minister's power to amend the First Schedule (s 6) beyond the list as it stands, the evidential
-- rule in s 2(4) and s 3(2) (a Gazette list conclusively proves inclusion), the s 4(a) construction of "governing body",
-- and anything that depends on the law of diplomatic immunity, which the Act borrows ("the like immunity ... as is
-- accorded to an envoy") but does not state. No order made under the Act was retrieved, so whether any organisation or
-- person actually holds any immunity today is a fact this encoding takes as an input.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `International Organisations (Immunities and Privileges) Act 1948 -- immunities`

§§ `2(1) and First Schedule -- which organisations`

-- s 2(1): "This section applies to (a) any organisation declared by an order of the President to be an organisation of
-- which the Government and the government or governments of one or more foreign sovereign Powers are members; (b) any
-- organisation specified in the First Schedule." First Schedule: 1. International Tribunal for the Law of the Sea.
-- 2. Bank for International Settlements. 3. Organisation for Economic Co-operation and Development [S 4/2025].
DECLARE Organisation IS ONE OF
    `the International Tribunal for the Law of the Sea`
    `the Bank for International Settlements`
    `the Organisation for Economic Co-operation and Development`
    `an organisation the President has declared under s 2(1)(a)`
    `a foreign charity or industry association`

GIVEN `the organisation` IS AN Organisation
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 2 applies to the organisation` IF
    CONSIDER `the organisation`
    WHEN `a foreign charity or industry association` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

§§ `2(2)(a) and Second Schedule Part 1 -- what an organisation may be given`

-- s 2(2)(a): the President "may by order provide that any organisation to which this section applies ... shall, TO SUCH
-- EXTENT AS MAY BE SPECIFIED IN THE ORDER, have the immunities and privileges set out in Part 1 of the Second Schedule,
-- and shall also have the legal capacities of a body corporate".
-- Part 1: 1. "Immunity from suit and legal process." 2. inviolability of official archives and office premises like an
-- envoy's. 3. "The like exemption or relief from taxes and rates, OTHER THAN import, export or excise duties on any
-- article or articles, as may be accorded to a foreign sovereign Power." 4. "Exemption from import or excise duties on any
-- article or articles directly imported by the organisation FOR ITS OFFICIAL USE in Singapore, such exemption to be SUBJECT
-- TO COMPLIANCE with such conditions as the Director-General of Customs may prescribe". 5. exemption from import and
-- export prohibitions for goods directly imported or exported for official use, and for its publications. 6. reduced
-- press-telegram rates for press and broadcast matter.
--
-- Being listed in the First Schedule is not enough: nothing is had until an order confers it. Export duties appear in the
-- exclusion in item 3 but in no exemption, so no order under Part 1 can relieve an organisation of an export duty.
DECLARE OrganisationBenefit IS ONE OF
    `immunity from suit and legal process`
    `inviolability of official archives and office premises`
    `relief from taxes and rates`
    `exemption from import duty on goods imported for official use`
    `exemption from excise duty on goods imported for official use`
    `exemption from import duty on goods not for official use`
    `exemption from export duty`
    `exemption from import and export prohibitions for official goods`
    `reduced press telegram rates`
    `the legal capacities of a body corporate`

GIVEN `the benefit` IS AN OrganisationBenefit
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the benefit is available under s 2(2)(a)` IF
    CONSIDER `the benefit`
    WHEN `exemption from import duty on goods not for official use` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `exemption from export duty` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

GIVEN `the organisation` IS AN Organisation, `the benefit` IS AN OrganisationBenefit, `an order confers it` IS A BOOLEAN, `customs conditions are complied with` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the organisation has the benefit` IF
        `section 2 applies to the organisation` `the organisation`
    AND `an order confers it`
    AND `the benefit is available under s 2(2)(a)` `the benefit`
    AND CONSIDER `the benefit`
        WHEN `exemption from import duty on goods imported for official use` THEN `customs conditions are complied with`
        WHEN `exemption from excise duty on goods imported for official use` THEN `customs conditions are complied with`
        OTHERWISE TRUE

§§ `2(2)(b), (c) and Second Schedule Parts 2 to 4 -- the organisation's people`

-- s 2(2)(b): the order may confer Part 2 on "(i) any persons who are representatives (whether of governments or not) on
-- any organ of the organisation or are members of any committee ...; (ii) such number of officers ... being the holders of
-- such HIGH offices ... as may be specified ...; and (iii) such persons employed on missions on behalf of the organisation
-- as may be so specified". (c): on "such OTHER classes of officers and employees ... as may be specified", Part 3.
-- "and Part 4 ... shall have effect for the purpose of extending to the staff of such representatives and members as are
-- mentioned in paragraph (b)(i) and to the families of officers ... any immunities and privileges conferred ... under
-- paragraph (b), EXCEPT insofar as the operation of Part 4 ... is excluded by the order".
-- Part 4 para 1: the representative's or member's "official staff ACCOMPANYING him as such"; para 2: an entitled officer's
-- "wife or husband and children UNDER THE AGE OF 21 YEARS".
--
-- Part 4 para 2 speaks of a person entitled "as an officer of the organisation". The encoding reads that as the high
-- officers in (b)(ii), so a family member of a person on a mission under (b)(iii) gets nothing (an inference: the text
-- names officers, not persons on missions). The "order confers" input stands for the order covering the principal.
DECLARE Role IS ONE OF
    `a representative on an organ`
    `a member of a committee`
    `a specified high officer`
    `a person on a specified mission`
    `an officer or employee of a specified class`
    `official staff of a representative or committee member`
    `the spouse of a high officer`
    `a child of a high officer`
    `a family member of a person on a mission`
    `a member of the public`

DECLARE SchedulePart IS ONE OF
    `Part 2`
    `Part 2 extended by Part 4`
    `Part 3`
    `no Part`

DECLARE Person HAS
    `role` IS A Role
    `age` IS A NUMBER
    `an order covers the person or principal` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the order excludes Part 4` IS A BOOLEAN
    `accompanying the principal` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the person` IS A Person
GIVETH A SchedulePart
DECIDE `the Part that applies` IS
    IF NOT `the person`'s `an order covers the person or principal`
    THEN `no Part`
    ELSE CONSIDER `the person`'s `role`
         WHEN `a representative on an organ` THEN `Part 2`
         WHEN `a member of a committee` THEN `Part 2`
         WHEN `a specified high officer` THEN `Part 2`
         WHEN `a person on a specified mission` THEN `Part 2`
         WHEN `an officer or employee of a specified class` THEN `Part 3`
         WHEN `official staff of a representative or committee member` THEN
             IF (NOT `the person`'s `the order excludes Part 4`) AND `the person`'s `accompanying the principal`
             THEN `Part 2 extended by Part 4`
             ELSE `no Part`
         WHEN `the spouse of a high officer` THEN
             IF NOT `the person`'s `the order excludes Part 4`
             THEN `Part 2 extended by Part 4`
             ELSE `no Part`
         WHEN `a child of a high officer` THEN
             IF (NOT `the person`'s `the order excludes Part 4`) AND `the person`'s `age` < 21
             THEN `Part 2 extended by Part 4`
             ELSE `no Part`
         OTHERWISE `no Part`

-- Part 2: 1. "The like immunity from suit and legal process as is accorded to an envoy of a foreign sovereign Power";
-- 2. "The like inviolability of residence"; 3. "The like exemption or relief from taxes".
-- Part 3: 1. "Immunity from suit and legal process IN RESPECT OF THINGS DONE OR OMITTED TO BE DONE IN THE COURSE OF THE
-- PERFORMANCE OF OFFICIAL DUTIES." 2. "Exemption from income tax in respect of emoluments received as an officer or
-- employee of the organisation."
--
-- Part 2 immunity is not limited to official acts in this Act; its extent is an envoy's, which the Act does not define.
-- The encoding therefore treats a Part 2 holder as immune whatever the claim is about, subject to the law of diplomatic
-- immunity (not encoded). Part 3 stops at official duties: a staff member's private debts and accidents are suable.
GIVEN `the person` IS A Person, `the claim concerns official duties` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person is immune from the suit` IF
    CONSIDER `the Part that applies` `the person`
    WHEN `Part 2` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `Part 2 extended by Part 4` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `Part 3` THEN `the claim concerns official duties`
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `the person` IS A Person
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person's residence is inviolable` IF
    CONSIDER `the Part that applies` `the person`
    WHEN `Part 2` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `Part 2 extended by Part 4` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `the person` IS A Person
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Act exempts the person's salary from the organisation from income tax` IF
    CONSIDER `the Part that applies` `the person`
    WHEN `Part 3` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `2(2) proviso -- no more than an agreement requires`

-- Proviso: "the order shall be so framed as to secure that there are not conferred on any person any immunities or
-- privileges GREATER in extent than those which, at the time of the making of the order, are REQUIRED to be conferred on
-- that person in order to give effect to any international agreement in that behalf."
GIVEN `the order confers the immunity` IS A BOOLEAN, `an international agreement required it when the order was made` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the order goes beyond the proviso` IF
    `the order confers the immunity` AND (NOT `an international agreement required it when the order was made`)

§§ `2(3) -- the Gazette lists`

-- s 2(3)(a): the President "SHALL compile a list of the persons entitled to immunities and privileges conferred under
-- subsection (2)(b), and MAY compile a list of the persons entitled ... under subsection (2)(c)"; (b) publish it in the
-- Gazette; (c) amend it as people come and go.
DECLARE ConferringParagraph IS ONE OF
    `s 2(2)(b)`
    `s 2(2)(c)`

GIVEN `the paragraph` IS A ConferringParagraph
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a Gazette list must be compiled` IF
    CONSIDER `the paragraph`
    WHEN `s 2(2)(b)` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `3 -- conferences held in Singapore`

-- s 3(1): where a conference "is held in Singapore and is attended by the representatives of the Government and the
-- government or governments of one or more foreign sovereign Powers" and doubts may arise, the President "MAY" publish a
-- list; and "every representative of a foreign Power who is for the time being included in the list shall ... be treated
-- as if he were such an envoy, and such of the members of his official staff as are ... included in the list shall be
-- treated ... as if they were his retinue."
--
-- No list, no status: the section works only through the published list, and the list is discretionary.
DECLARE ConferenceRole IS ONE OF
    `a representative of a foreign Power`
    `official staff of a foreign representative`
    `a representative of the Singapore Government`
    `a delegate of a non-governmental body`

DECLARE ConferenceStatus IS ONE OF
    `treated as an envoy`
    `treated as an envoy's retinue`
    `no status under s 3`

GIVEN `the role` IS A ConferenceRole, `held in Singapore with the Government and a foreign government attending` IS A BOOLEAN, `on the published list` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A ConferenceStatus
DECIDE `the conference status` IS
    IF (NOT `held in Singapore with the Government and a foreign government attending`) OR (NOT `on the published list`)
    THEN `no status under s 3`
    ELSE CONSIDER `the role`
         WHEN `a representative of a foreign Power` THEN `treated as an envoy`
         WHEN `official staff of a foreign representative` THEN `treated as an envoy's retinue`
         OTHERWISE `no status under s 3`

§§ `4(b) -- the International Court`

-- s 4(b): in its application to the United Nations, "the powers conferred by section 2(2) include power by order to confer
-- on the JUDGES AND REGISTRARS of the International Court and on SUITORS to that Court and their AGENTS, COUNSEL AND
-- ADVOCATES, such immunities, privileges and facilities as may be required to give effect to any resolution of, or
-- convention approved by, the General Assembly".
DECLARE CourtRole IS ONE OF
    `a judge of the International Court`
    `a registrar of the International Court`
    `a suitor to the International Court`
    `counsel for a suitor`
    `a journalist covering the Court`

GIVEN `the court role` IS A CourtRole
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an order under s 4(b) may reach the person` IF
    CONSIDER `the court role`
    WHEN `a journalist covering the Court` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

§§ `5 -- reciprocity`

-- s 5: nothing in ss 2 to 4 precludes the President "from declining to accord immunities or privileges to, or from
-- withdrawing immunities or privileges from, nationals or representatives of any Power on the ground that that Power is
-- failing to accord corresponding immunities or privileges to Singapore nationals or representatives."
GIVEN `the Power fails to accord corresponding immunities to Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the President may withhold on the ground of reciprocity` IF
    `the Power fails to accord corresponding immunities to Singapore`
